# Shannon Clone — Cursor Agent Rules

## Project
AI-powered security scanner. Next.js 15 + Trigger.dev v3 + Vercel AI SDK v6 + SQLite.
No auth for now. All agents are in /trigger/.

## Stack rules
- Use `streamText` from `ai` with `maxSteps: 10000` for ALL agent loops
- Use `anthropic('claude-sonnet-4-6')` as the model
- All background tasks use `@trigger.dev/sdk` task()
- DB uses Prisma with SQLite (file:./dev.db) — no Postgres
- No auth middleware — skip it entirely for now
- Tools are defined with `tool()` from `ai` and typed with `zod`

## File structure
- /trigger/          → all 13 agent task files
- /trigger/agents/base-agent.ts  → shared runAgent() helper
- /trigger/tools/index.ts        → all Claude tools
- /lib/prompt-manager.ts         → loads prompts from Shannon repo
- /prisma/schema.prisma          → SQLite schema

## Agent pattern (always use this)
```typescript
import { streamText, tool } from 'ai';
import { anthropic } from '@ai-sdk/anthropic';

const result = await streamText({
  model: anthropic('claude-sonnet-4-6'),
  system: systemPrompt,
  prompt: userPrompt,
  tools: { readFile, searchRepo, httpRequest },
  maxSteps: 10000,
  onStepFinish: (step) => logger.info('step', step),
});
```

## Prompt loading
Prompts come from Shannon's repo. Load like this:
```typescript
const BASE = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/KeygraphHQ/shannon/main/prompts';
const text = await fetch(`${BASE}/vuln-xss.txt`).then(r => r.text());
```
Variables use {{TARGET_URL}}, {{CONFIG_CONTEXT}} syntax.

## DB schema (key models)
- Scan: id, targetUrl, repoPath, status, findings(Json), report(Json)
- Finding: id, scanId, type, severity, title, endpoint, payload, evidence

## Tool definitions
All tools use `tool({ description, parameters: z.object({...}), execute })` pattern.
Tools available: readFile, searchRepo, httpRequest, runBrowser, reportFinding, analyzeAST

## Build order
1. prisma/schema.prisma
2. Run `npx prisma migrate dev --name init`
3. Run `npx prisma generate`
4. lib/prompt-manager.ts
5. trigger/agents/base-agent.ts
6. trigger/tools/index.ts
7. trigger/agents/agent-0-pre-recon.ts
8. trigger/agents/agent-1-recon.ts
9. trigger/agents/agent-2-vuln.ts
10. trigger/agents/agent-3-exploit.ts
11. trigger/agents/agent-4-report.ts
12. trigger/scan.ts (orchestrator)

## UI
13. app/api/scan/start/route.ts
14. app/api/scan/[id]/route.ts
15. app/(dashboard)/scans/page.tsx
16. app/(dashboard)/scans/[id]/page.tsx


## Offensive tools (Docker worker only)
All CLI tools run via execCommandTool from /trigger/tools/exec-command.ts.
NEVER run execSync directly in a task — always go through execCommandTool.
Allowed tools: nmap, httpx, ffuf, nuclei, sqlmap, gobuster, curl, jwt_tool.
Tools run inside Docker with NET_RAW + NET_ADMIN capabilities.
All tool output is capped at 10000 chars and logged via logger.info.

## Tool → agent mapping
- nmap, httpx, ffuf, gobuster → phase-1-recon.ts only
- nuclei → phase-2-vuln.ts (all 5 agents)
- sqlmap → phase-3-exploit.ts (injection agent only)
- playwright → phase-3-exploit.ts (xss, auth, idor agents)
- jwt_tool → phase-3-exploit.ts (auth agent only)
- curl → phase-3-exploit.ts (ssrf agent only)